# Rail-optimized 128-GPU compute fabric for the Ofan MoE study, 2-tier leaf-spine.
#
#   128 GPUs = 16 servers x 8 GPUs; each GPU has its own 800G NIC -> its own rail.
#   8 rails; rail r is ONE leaf with 16 downlinks (GPU r of all 16 servers) + 16
#   uplinks => 32-port leaf. 8 leaves, 16 spines of radix 8, NON-BLOCKING.
#   Links 800 Gbps, 0.5 us (the Ofan paper's link parameters).
#
#   "Rails 8": GPU g -> rail (g%8), server (g/8), leaf = rail.
#   DeepEP-style dispatch sends every inter-server flow to the SAME-RANK GPU, i.e.
#   the same rail, so all fabric traffic stays on one leaf (never touches a spine).
#   Intra-server traffic goes over the NVLink plane (nvlink_128gpu_8pergpu.topo),
#   selected at connect time by htsim when -nvlink_topo is given.
#   Pattern copied from shared/topos_h100/rail_1024gpu_8rail.topo.
Nodes 128
Tiers 2
Podsize 128
Rails 8

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 800
Radix_Down 16
Radix_Up 16
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 800
Radix_Down 8
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1
